9. Why Google Gemini?
Google Gemini was selected because it provides generative AI capabilities that can understand natural-language questions and generate contextual responses.
For EduGenie, Gemini can be used for:
Question answering
Summarization
Explanation
Content generation
Quiz generation
Personalized learning assistance
The AI model becomes the core intelligence of the application.
10. User Journey
The planned user journey is:
Step 1 – Open EduGenie
The student opens the learning assistant.
Step 2 – Enter a question
The student types a question or learning request.
Step 3 – Request processing
The application sends the request to the Gemini-powered backend.
Step 4 – AI processing
Gemini understands the request and generates an appropriate response.
Step 5 – Display response
The response is displayed to the student in an easy-to-read format.
Step 6 – Further interaction
The student can ask follow-up questions for deeper understanding.
11. Example Use Case
Scenario:
A BCA student is studying Data Structures and does not understand a binary tree.
The student enters:
"Explain binary tree in simple words with an example."
EduGenie processes the request using Gemini.
The system can respond with:
Definition of binary tree
Basic terminology
Simple diagram/example
Types of binary trees
Important exam points
The student can then ask:
"Give me a 5-mark answer."
EduGenie can generate an answer in the requested format.
